      "side": 1,
      "message": "Things go wrong in av1/encoder/svc_layercontext.c:\n\n```\nvoid av1_update_temporal_layer_framerate(AV1_COMP *const cpi) {\n  ...\n  lc-\u003eframerate \u003d cpi-\u003eframerate / lc-\u003eframerate_factor;\n  lrc-\u003eavg_frame_bandwidth \u003d (int)round(lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth / lc-\u003eframerate);\n```\n\n   cpi-\u003eframerate\u003d0.462339, lc-\u003eframerate_factor\u003d4\n   lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth\u003d276824000, lc-\u003eframerate\u003d0.115585\n   \nI added a `saturate_cast_double_to_int()` function to handle this case. Plase replace the `(int)` cast before the `round()` call with `saturate_cast_double_to_int()`.\n\nWe may want to fix other instances of this pattern. I ran the command:\n\n```\nfind . -name \"*\" -a -type f | xargs grep target_bandwidth | grep framerate\n```\n\nand found the following:\n\n```\n./av1/encoder/ratectrl.c:        (int)round(lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth / lc-\u003eframerate) - encoded_frame_size;\n./av1/encoder/ratectrl.c:      1, (int)(oxcf-\u003erc_cfg.target_bandwidth / oxcf-\u003einput_cfg.init_framerate));\n./av1/encoder/ratectrl.c:      1, (int)(oxcf-\u003erc_cfg.target_bandwidth / oxcf-\u003einput_cfg.init_framerate));\n./av1/encoder/ratectrl.c:      round(oxcf-\u003erc_cfg.target_bandwidth / cpi-\u003eframerate));\n./av1/encoder/svc_layercontext.c:          (int)round(lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth / lc-\u003eframerate);\n./av1/encoder/svc_layercontext.c:  lrc-\u003eavg_frame_bandwidth \u003d (int)round(lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth / lc-\u003eframerate);\n./av1/encoder/svc_layercontext.c:      lc-\u003eavg_frame_size \u003d (int)round(lc-\u003etarget_bandwidth / lc-\u003eframerate);\n```",
